### 18. ROW LEVEL SECURITY AND BACKEND SECURITY

Enable RLS on all tables exposed through Supabase APIs.

Write and test explicit policies.

At minimum:

- Users can access and update only permitted fields in their own profiles.
- Users can read only their own private discovery answers, conversations, memories, recommendations, and progress.
- Public profile fields are accessible only according to visibility settings.
- Connection requests can be read or modified only by authorized participants.
- Messages are accessible only to authorized conversation participants.
- Community posts and comments follow community visibility and membership rules.
- Experts can access only mentoring records and conversations they are authorized to see.
- Administrators receive privileged access only through a secure, verifiable authorization mechanism.
- Users cannot assign themselves privileged roles or bypass approval requirements.
- Reports and audit logs are protected from unauthorized modification.
- Anonymous users cannot access private user records.

Also implement:

- Server-side input validation.
- Output escaping and safe rendering of user-generated content.
- Rate limiting for AI calls, messaging, and sensitive endpoints.
- Appropriate request-size limits.
- Safe error messages without stack traces or secrets.
- Authentication checks in every privileged Edge Function.
- Secure OAuth configuration.
- Protection against prompt injection and malicious user-generated content.
- No execution of instructions found in user-submitted text as trusted system instructions.

Never rely solely on hidden UI elements to enforce permissions.

