### 28. FINAL PRODUCT PRINCIPLE

Throughout development, keep returning to this question:

**"Will this feature help a person understand themselves better, explore an interest, connect with the right people, or decide what to do next?"**

If a feature does not contribute meaningfully to that goal, simplify it or postpone it.

Skill Path should not pressure people to choose a career prematurely. It should help them discover, experiment, reflect, and grow.

The final experience should leave a user thinking:

"I may not know my entire future yet, but I understand myself better, I have discovered something worth exploring, and I know what I can do next."

Build Skill Path to deliver that experience through a secure, usable, maintainable, and genuinely functional application.
